<% content_for :title, "Installation" %>

<div class="mb-8">
  <p class="mb-2 text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-primary">Getting Started</p>
  <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight mb-3">Installation</h1>
  <p class="text-muted-foreground">Add rails-ui-kit to your Rails app in four steps.</p>
</div>

<div class="mb-10 rounded-lg border border-border bg-muted px-5 py-4">
  <p class="text-sm text-neutral-600 dark:text-neutral-400">
    <span class="font-semibold text-neutral-900 dark:text-neutral-100">Requires Tailwind CSS 4</span>, through
    <code class="text-xs bg-neutral-100 dark:bg-neutral-800 px-1 py-0.5 rounded font-mono">tailwindcss-rails</code> 4.x.
    Every colour and radius in the kit comes from design tokens that only a Tailwind 4 build can compile — there is no
    Tailwind 3, PostCSS or Sprockets path for them.
  </p>
</div>

<div class="space-y-10">

  <div>
    <h2 class="flex items-center gap-3 text-lg font-semibold mb-4">
      <span class="flex h-6 w-6 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-neutral-900 dark:bg-white text-white dark:text-neutral-900 text-xs font-bold">1</span>
      Add to your Gemfile
    </h2>
    <div class="rounded-lg overflow-hidden border border-neutral-800">
      <div class="flex items-center justify-between bg-neutral-900 px-4 py-2">
        <span class="text-xs text-neutral-400">Gemfile</span>
        <button data-copy-target="#install-gem" class="text-xs text-neutral-400 hover:text-white transition-colors">Copy</button>
      </div>
      <pre class="bg-neutral-950 px-5 py-4 overflow-x-auto text-sm leading-relaxed" tabindex="0"><code id="install-gem" class="text-neutral-200">gem "rails-ui-kit", git: "git@github.com:productmatter/rails-ui-kit.git", branch: "main"</code></pre>
    </div>
    <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-muted-foreground">Then run <code class="text-xs bg-neutral-100 dark:bg-neutral-800 px-1 py-0.5 rounded">bundle install</code>.</p>
  </div>

  <div>
    <h2 class="flex items-center gap-3 text-lg font-semibold mb-4">
      <span class="flex h-6 w-6 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-neutral-900 dark:bg-white text-white dark:text-neutral-900 text-xs font-bold">2</span>
      Run the install generator
    </h2>
    <div class="rounded-lg overflow-hidden border border-neutral-800">
      <div class="flex items-center justify-between bg-neutral-900 px-4 py-2">
        <span class="text-xs text-neutral-400">Terminal</span>
        <button data-copy-target="#install-gen" class="text-xs text-neutral-400 hover:text-white transition-colors">Copy</button>
      </div>
      <pre class="bg-neutral-950 px-5 py-4 overflow-x-auto text-sm leading-relaxed" tabindex="0"><code id="install-gen" class="text-neutral-200">bin/rails generate rails_ui_kit:install</code></pre>
    </div>
    <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-muted-foreground">
      This wires the JavaScript controllers into <code class="text-xs bg-neutral-100 dark:bg-neutral-800 px-1 py-0.5 rounded">application.js</code>,
      imports the built CSS into your Tailwind entry point, and adds
      <code class="text-xs bg-neutral-100 dark:bg-neutral-800 px-1 py-0.5 rounded font-mono">@custom-variant dark (&amp;:where(.dark, .dark *));</code>
      so Tailwind's <code class="text-xs bg-neutral-100 dark:bg-neutral-800 px-1 py-0.5 rounded font-mono">dark:</code> utilities follow the same
      <code class="text-xs bg-neutral-100 dark:bg-neutral-800 px-1 py-0.5 rounded font-mono">.dark</code> class the kit's tokens do, rather than the
      OS preference. If your stylesheet already defines a dark variant, the generator leaves it alone and says so.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div>
    <h2 class="flex items-center gap-3 text-lg font-semibold mb-4">
      <span class="flex h-6 w-6 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-neutral-900 dark:bg-white text-white dark:text-neutral-900 text-xs font-bold">3</span>
      Set up your layout
    </h2>
    <p class="text-sm text-neutral-600 dark:text-neutral-400 mb-3">
      Put <code class="text-xs bg-neutral-100 dark:bg-neutral-800 px-1 py-0.5 rounded font-mono">bg-background text-foreground</code> on
      <code class="text-xs bg-neutral-100 dark:bg-neutral-800 px-1 py-0.5 rounded font-mono">&lt;body&gt;</code>. The kit paints no page colour
      of its own, so without it your page keeps the browser's white under dark-mode components, and kit surfaces won't match the page around them.
      Then render the singletons once — they provide the global confirm dialog, toast stack, and utility controllers.
    </p>
    <div class="rounded-lg overflow-hidden border border-neutral-800">
      <div class="flex items-center justify-between bg-neutral-900 px-4 py-2">
        <span class="text-xs text-neutral-400">app/views/layouts/application.html.erb</span>
        <button data-copy-target="#install-layout" class="text-xs text-neutral-400 hover:text-white transition-colors">Copy</button>
      </div>
      <pre class="bg-neutral-950 px-5 py-4 overflow-x-auto text-sm leading-relaxed" tabindex="0"><code id="install-layout" class="text-neutral-200">&lt;body class="bg-background text-foreground"&gt;
  &lt;%= render Ui::ConfirmDialogComponent.new %&gt;
  &lt;%= render Ui::ToastContainerComponent.new %&gt;
  &lt;div data-controller="ui--turbo-confirm ui--turbo-disable-with"&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
  &lt;%= yield %&gt;
&lt;/body&gt;</code></pre>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div>
    <h2 class="flex items-center gap-3 text-lg font-semibold mb-4">
      <span class="flex h-6 w-6 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-neutral-900 dark:bg-white text-white dark:text-neutral-900 text-xs font-bold">4</span>
      Install peer dependencies
    </h2>
    <p class="text-sm text-neutral-600 dark:text-neutral-400 mb-3">
      Dropdown, Tooltip, and Popover require <code class="text-xs bg-neutral-100 dark:bg-neutral-800 px-1 py-0.5 rounded">@floating-ui/dom</code>.
      If you're using importmap (the default), it's already pinned for you. For bundler setups:
    </p>
    <div class="rounded-lg overflow-hidden border border-neutral-800">
      <div class="flex items-center justify-between bg-neutral-900 px-4 py-2">
        <span class="text-xs text-neutral-400">Terminal</span>
        <button data-copy-target="#install-npm" class="text-xs text-neutral-400 hover:text-white transition-colors">Copy</button>
      </div>
      <pre class="bg-neutral-950 px-5 py-4 overflow-x-auto text-sm leading-relaxed" tabindex="0"><code id="install-npm" class="text-neutral-200">npm install @floating-ui/dom @hotwired/stimulus</code></pre>
    </div>
  </div>

</div>
